  "narrative": {
    "intro": "United Parcel Service has $56.4M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. United Parcel Service received 210 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $269K, and obligations are down 61.1% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, accounting for $55.3M of FY2027 obligations. Obligations by fiscal year were $238M in FY22, $230M in FY23, $345M in FY24, $198M in FY25, $145M in FY26, and $56.4M in FY27. The current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date activity. The top buying agencies after the Department of Veterans Affairs are the Department of Commerce at $1000K and the Department of Homeland Security at $93.5K, followed by several smaller agency buyers. These figures are contract obligations except where noted otherwise for award values in award tables. The picture for FY2027 to date shows a concentrated set of obligations tied heavily to one agency and a marked decline in obligations compared with the prior year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are United Parcel Service federal obligations in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "United Parcel Service obligations are highly concentrated in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $55.3M, which represents the vast majority of the $56.4M total. The remaining obligations are spread across several agencies at much smaller amounts. The concentration indicates most FY2027 activity ties to one buyer."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has United Parcel Service federal business moved over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "United Parcel Service obligations rose and fell across the last five fiscal years. Obligations were $238M in FY22, $230M in FY23, $345M in FY24, $198M in FY25, $145M in FY26, and $56.4M in FY27. FY2027 to date obligations are down 61.1% year over year. The average award size in FY2027 to date is $269K across 210 awards."
      }
    ]
  },
